Cell["\<\
Below the threshold the most visited extension is far from a segment; at the \
threshold the excess drops to zero and stays there. The most visited member \
jumps from a walk near the germ to a segment.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e1e7350d-d83b-4ddc-8448-de27a0e1d706"],

Cell["\<\
The triangular tiling straightens first, then the square tiling, then the \
hexagonal tiling.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ee140844-3d3b-41fb-b1ba-5b435c9d9fb0"],

Cell["\<\
On the square and the triangular tilings the deviation falls at the same \
threshold to a floor, the staircase of a segment off the lattice directions. \
On the hexagonal tiling it falls only a little and grows again: a straight \
extension zigzags almost as far from its chord as a bent one.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f135409f-5e89-458a-9326-a0a9e7efc5ad"],

Cell["Open questions", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c2396d59-26b2-4c9a-9734-325a3e4ece7c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "[[ The inextensible geodesic at scale ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d8360088-bf4b-4067-a6e1-606cc96ede00"],
 " as an object: the infinite walks of the window graph from the germ's \
window. Is its most visited member eventually a ray at every scale above ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "*"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "af69559d-e754-4b1e-a18d-38492b9b9507"],
 ", and how does ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "*"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0ceba404-9149-49d1-8510-979cb22ae94a"],
 " depend on the length of the germ? ]]"
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"9c255df0-cd7b-447b-a966-a0f51ff9bdbf"],

Cell["\<\
[[ The loss of direction on a lattice: the straight members follow the cone, \
not the germ. Does a mesh or a sprinkling, with no preferred directions, \
restore the germ's direction at large scales? ]]\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"21bfea3e-8e79-431f-a82b-9c375d67e0db"],

